## Concrete correction to hand to the builder

At the catalogue observation boundary, supply a same-family comparison, not a winner inferred from retrieval score. For a SKU/code request:

- score means lexical retrieval only. A strict score lead is not proof of a unique variant.
- Compare original user constraints with actual sibling names and properties. A qualifier absent from all records remains unresolved; never silently discard it. Word absence does not establish a negative property. Generic packaging/kind words do not eliminate siblings unless actual attributes justify it.
- OK only after evidence identifies one compatible product. An exact verified SKU remains a valid direct answer even when siblings exist. If several compatible variants remain, ask about their distinguishing attribute; put their SKU codes in message and paths in refs.
- Incomplete top-N/index evidence cannot establish uniqueness. Continue narrow retrieval or keep uncertainty; do not set pool_complete from indexed_products alone.
- Preserve security, exclusion, stock/yes-no and mutation policy routing. This is a catalogue-resolution correction, not an outcome rewrite for every task mentioning SKU.

Ready research helper: [lookup_evidence.py](../experiments/2026-10-22-codex-sol-61-sku-clarification-contract/lookup_evidence.py), d4922r1. It computes per-token support and groups visible families with their sibling records from a supplied current-world product pool. Add its result as a catalogue observation field (e.g. sku_lookup_evidence), preserving the original matches/ranking. Pass explicit collector completeness; captured top8 snapshots in this experiment correctly use false. The helper changes no answers, invents no head-design field, and does not implement an intent parser. A shipping port needs context-size limits with an explicit truncation flag and verified index coverage; keep this reference helper out of agent.py until that bounded port is reviewed. The decision_rule field contains the concrete model instruction to port.

Minimal target outcome: on the frozen Metabo request, stop treating head's lexical hit as a unique standard-head product. Ask which compatible configuration the user needs. Do not hard-code Metabo, family names, task numbers, standard/head word tables or the graded SKU. The names here are evidence, never branch conditions.

